diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..fbc1070 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -2,6 +2,36 @@
 
 Webhooks notify another application when something happens on a board. Only account admins can list, view, create, update, delete, or reactivate webhooks.
 
+When an event a webhook is subscribed to happens, we `POST` the event to the payload URL exactly once and log
+how it went. Deliveries are logged for a week and then removed.
+
+Each request carries these headers:
+
+| Header | Value |
+| --- | --- |
+| `User-Agent` | `fizzy/1.0.0 Webhook` |
+| `Content-Type` | `application/json` |
+| `X-Webhook-Timestamp` | When the event happened |
+| `X-Webhook-Signature` | `HMAC-SHA256` of the request body, keyed with the webhook's `signing_secret` |
+
+The body is the event, with its `board`, `creator`, and `eventable` (a card or a comment):
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohde",
+  "action": "card_closed",
+  "created_at": "2025-12-05T19:36:35.401Z",
+  "eventable": { "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohdb", "title": "Design the logo", "url": "https://app.fizzy.do/897362094/cards/1" },
+  "board": { "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohcy", "name": "Fizzy" },
+  "creator": { "id": "03f5v9zjw7pz8717a4no1h8a7", "name": "David Heinemeier Hansson" }
+}
+```
+
+Payload URLs pointing at Slack, Campfire, or Basecamp get a chat message instead of the full event.
+
+A receiver that keeps failing is switched off: ten failed deliveries in a row within an hour deactivate the
+webhook, and it stays off until someone reactivates it. Any successful delivery starts the count over.
+
 ## `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks`
 
 Returns a paginated list of webhooks for a board.
